# Normalise line endings so a checkout is byte-identical on every machine.
#
# Without this file each clone's core.autocrlf setting decides, and CRLF can
# reach the stored blob. That is what happened when the Maven wrapper was bumped
# in #7: mvnw.cmd landed with CRLF, and any clone configured to normalise on
# staging showed all 189 lines as modified straight after checkout. #23 undid it
# by hand. These rules stop it recurring rather than relying on every clone
# being configured the same way.
#
# text=auto stores every text file with LF whatever platform committed it.
# eol=lf checks it back out that way too, so the working tree matches across
# machines instead of differing by platform default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells are the one place CRLF still earns its keep: cmd.exe can
# mis-parse a batch file whose multi-line constructs end in bare LF. Only the
# checked-out copy gets CRLF -- the stored blob stays LF, which is what #23
# restored. nbastats/.gitattributes already sets this for the Maven wrapper;
# stated here too so it covers any .cmd or .bat added elsewhere later.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Declared rather than left to content sniffing, so a diff never tries to
# render them as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
